AIM Responsibilities:
Provide software to create Shipping labels based on the content of an HTTP POST request.  If there are exceptions, the exceptions will be written to the AIMVision\Lineside\Exceptions folder using the same name as the label number with a “.txt” extension when possible.  A message will also be written to the acsMobileLog Event Log.
 
 
Activities and Deliverables
Customer Activities
Provide two HTTP POST requests as outlined in Exhibit A   Provide network infrastructure to facilitate the HTTP POST request to the server
 
AIM Activities
Modify the AIM Mobility Web service to allow processing the HTTP POST request as described in this document.  The service will listen on the designated port, usually port 8080 to allow the application service to create a shipping label.  The label will not be printed from AIM but instead printed by the MPP MES system as it does today.  If exceptions occur, an exception will be created and written to the AIMVision\Lineside\Exceptions folder using the same name as the serial number when possible with a “.txt”.
 
Modify the AIM Mobility application service (MobileMain) to create a shipping label using the content of the HTTP POST request to locate an active blanket from the AIM Vision Orders system, using the quantity and supplier lot number based on the HTTP POST request content.  See Exhibit A for details of the HTTP POST request.

Constraints and Exclusions
Label types must be identified as Quick Label Allowed
Labels that require additional input are outside the scope of this project
Lot control is outside the scope of this project
The label content must be the same for a given Customer Part number issued from the floor. For example, if the same customer part is sent to multiple destinations and the label requires destination specific content, adjustments will have to be made and are considered outside the scope of this project.


Exhibit A – HTTP POST request and content
 
Two different POST requests will be used for the label creation.  The first request will be used when a label number is needed to get a unique 9 digit serial for a specific company code.  The second request will be used to fill in the label content.
 
Each request will be in the format
      http://{servername}:8080/mes/floor/{CompanyCode}/636652666553236784/{request}
 
{servername} is the name of the AIM Server (or IP address of the server).
{CompanyCode} is the company code defined in AIM. “99” is usually used for test.
{request} will be one of the following:
      nextserial.csv - used to request the next 9 digit serial number form the {CompanyCode}
      postserial.csv - used to create serial label using POST content
 
Serial Number Request/Reply
 
Request next Serial Number:
      http://{servername}:8080/mes/floor/{CompanyCode}/636652666553236784/nextserial.csv
 
Reply:
{serialnumber} – Nine digit unique per company code, (i.e. 123456789)
{cr} – carriage return (hex 0x0d)
{lf} – linefeed (hex 0x0a)
 
